# Line endings are part of a package's bytes.
#
# A capability package is built from these files and published as an archive pinned by
# SHA-256, and each target is built on its own platform. Left to Git's per-machine
# defaults, a Windows checkout would produce CRLF in every text file and a different
# archive for the same source — a reproducibility failure with no cause anyone could see
# in a diff. So the working tree gets LF everywhere, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything whose bytes are its meaning is never rewritten.
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.nodus-plugin binary
*.sig binary
